---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description="A clear, evidence-based guide to rent control, rent stabilization, and how they work — with a focus on New York and global examples."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="tagline">Housing policy, explained</p>
    <h1>Rent control doesn't have to be confusing.</h1>
    <p>
      Politicians, landlords, and pundits talk past each other on rent regulation.
      This site cuts through the noise: what the terms actually mean, how the
      policies work in practice, and what the evidence really says.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="card-grid">
    <a href="/definitions" class="card">
      <h2>Definitions</h2>
      <p>Rent control, rent stabilization, vacancy control — what each term means and why the difference matters.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/new-york" class="card">
      <h2>New York</h2>
      <p>How rent stabilization works in NYC: the Rent Guidelines Board, the 2019 reforms, and Mamdani's rent freeze proposal.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/examples" class="card">
      <h2>Examples</h2>
      <p>Germany, Minnesota, California, Spain — places where rent regulation didn't kill construction.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/resources" class="card">
      <h2>Resources</h2>
      <p>Academic papers, policy organizations, data sources, and further reading.</p>
    </a>
  </div>

  <hr />

  <div class="callout">
    <h3>Why this site exists</h3>
    <p>
      With Zaran Mamdani's election and his promise of a rent freeze, a lot of people
      are hearing about "rent control" for the first time — and most of what they hear
      is wrong. The goal here is to give you the facts, clearly and honestly, so you
      can make up your own mind.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
